          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            the
            %em type of propositions
            (
            %a{:href => "#UFP13"}> Univalent Foundations Project 2013
            ) or
            %em universe of propositions
            (
            %a{:href => "#AKX25"}> Altenkirch, Kaposi, &amp; Xie 2025
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AngiuliGratzer"} Angiuli &amp; Gratzer
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Prop
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            — corresponds, under
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
          %blockquote
            %p
              (To be precise, depending on the type theoretic rules and axioms this may not be quite true: one needs
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+resizing"} propositional resizing
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+extensionality"} propositional extensionality
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/calculus+of+constructions"} calculus of constructions
              — the
              = succeed ".)" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+unique+choice"} principle of unique choice
          %p
            Its generalization from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositions"} propositions
            to general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtypes"} subtypes
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            may typically be identified with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function+types"} function types
            into the type of propositions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sub
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Prop
                    %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≡
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Prop
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≡
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Ω
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sub(A)
                  \\;\;
                  \=
                  \\;\;
                  Prop_A
                  \\;\;
                  \\equiv
                  \\;\;
                  A \to Prop
                  \\;\;
                  \\equiv
                  \\;\;
                  A \to \Omega
                  \\,.
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            such a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \,\colon\, A \to Prop
            is equivalently an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type"} dependent
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proposition"} proposition
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/term"} term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \colon A
            the assertion that “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is contained in the given subtype”.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are many different ways of defining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isProp"} isProp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modality"} modality
            in dependent type theory. Some of them include
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}(A) \coloneqq \prod_{x:A} \prod_{y:A} x =_A y
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi A
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}(A) \coloneqq \prod_{x:A} \prod_{y:A} \mathrm{isContr}(x =_A y)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isContr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}(A) \coloneqq A \to \mathrm{isContr}(A)
          %p
            We shall be agnostic about the different definitions of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}(A)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{isProp}(A)
          %p
            The
            %strong type of (all) propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            could be defined in many different ways:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory+with+type+variables"} dependent type theory with type variables
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+polymorphism"} impredicative polymorphism
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+type"} positive
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive-inductive+type"} higher inductive-inductive type
                representing the homotopy-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/initial+object"} initial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
                or
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Heyting+algebra"} complete Heyting algebra
            %li
              %p
                as a homotopy-
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
                univalent family of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-propositions"} h-propositions
            %li
              %p
                as a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
                that mimic that of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+type"} negative
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+sum+type"} dependent sum type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo :
                          %mi U
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{P:U} \mathrm{isProp}(P)
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo :
                          %mi U
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{P:U} \mathrm{isProp}(T(P))
                respectively, but for all types, not just the
                = succeed "-small" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          %p
            In addition, in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            defined using a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+hierarchy"} universe hierarchy
            instead of a separate type judgment, a universe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            having the type of all propositions as defined above is equivalent to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
            axiom which says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+type"}
              locally
              = succeed "-small" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{P:U_i} \mathrm{isProp}(P)
            is (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+type"}> essentially
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+type"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
                \-small
          %h3#as_a_homotopyinitial_type As a homotopy-initial type
          %p
            Suppose that the dependent type theory has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+variables"} type variables
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+polymorphism"} impredicative polymorphism
            %strong type of (all) propositions
            can be defined as any of the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+inductive-inductive+types"} higher inductive-inductive types
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                As the (homotopy)-initial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}
            %li
              %p
                As the (homotopy)-initial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+Heyting+algebra"} complete Heyting algebra
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}
          %p
            since these structures can only be defined with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+polymorphism"} impredicative polymorphism
            in the absence of an already pre-existing type of all propositions. The Tarski universe type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\mathrm{Prop} \vdash \mathrm{El}(P)
            is given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification"} identification
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth"} truth
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mo ⊤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}(P) \coloneqq (P =_{\mathrm{Prop}} \top)
          %p and the Tarski universe is univalent by concatenation of identifications in the frame.
          %h3#as_a_homotopyterminal_type As a homotopy-terminal type
          %p
            A
            %strong univalent family of propositions
            consists of a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and a type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (B(x))_{x:A}
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(x)
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
                for all
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
                function
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} tr
                        %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi x
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi A
                      %mi y
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{tr}^B(x, y):x =_A y \to (B(x) \simeq B(y))
              %p
                is an
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:A
          %p
            A morphism of univalent families of propositions between univalent families of propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, B)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A', B')
            consists of a function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_A:A \to A'
            and a family of functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_B(x):B(x) \to B'(f_A(x))
          %p
            The
            %strong type of (all) propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathrm{Prop}, \mathrm{El})
            is the homotopy-terminal univalent family of propositions: given any other univalent family of propositions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A, B)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi u
                    %mi A
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_A:A \to \mathrm{Prop}
            and a unique family of functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi u
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u_B(x):B(x) \to \mathrm{El}(u_A(x))
          %h3#as_a_type_universe As a type universe
          %p
            The
            %strong type of (all) propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            of all
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+propositions"} mere propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/record+type"} record type
            where one of the fields is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a type
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \; \mathrm{type}
            %li
              %p
                a witness
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\mathrm{isProp}(A)
                that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
          %p
            Similar to other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universes"} type universes
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/record+types+with+type+fields"} record types with type fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Tarski"} a la Tarski
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Russell"} a la Russell
          %h4#a_la_tarski A la Tarski
          %p
            The type of all propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Tarski"} a la Tarski
            is given by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
            (see
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "#AngiuliGratzer"} Angiuli &amp; Gratzer
          %p Formation rules for the type of all propositions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{Prop} \; \mathrm{type}}
          %p Introduction rules for the type of all propositions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toProp
                        %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{toProp}_A:\mathrm{isProp}(A) \to \mathrm{Prop}}
          %p Elimination rules for the type of all propositions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                  %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} proptrunc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{Prop}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{El}(A) \; \mathrm{type}} \qquad \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{Prop}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{proptrunc}(A):\mathrm{isProp}(\mathrm{El}(A))}
          %p Computation rules for the type of all propositions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toProp
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash p:\mathrm{isProp}(A)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{El}(\mathrm{toProp}_A(p)) \equiv A \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} proptrunc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toProp
                        %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≡
                      %mi p
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A \; \mathrm{type} \quad \Gamma \vdash p:\mathrm{isProp}(A)}{\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{proptrunc}(\mathrm{toProp}_A(p)) \equiv p:\mathrm{isProp}(A)}
          %p Uniqueness rules for the type of all propositions:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≡
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} toProp
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} proptrunc
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{Prop}}{\Gamma \vdash A \equiv \mathrm{toProp}_{\mathrm{El}(A)}(\mathrm{proptrunc}(A)):\mathrm{Prop}}
          %p
            Extensionality principle of the type of all propositions (i.e.
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+extensionality"} propositional extensionality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi A
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %msub
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ext
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} transport
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \vdash A:\mathrm{Prop} \quad \Gamma \vdash B:\mathrm{Prop}} {\Gamma \vdash \mathrm{ext}_\mathrm{Prop}(A, B):\mathrm{isEquiv}(\mathrm{transport}^\mathrm{El}(A, B))}
          %h4#a_la_russell A la Russell
          %p
            The type of all propositions
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/a+la+Russell"} a la Russell
            is given by the following
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+deduction"} natural deduction
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inference+rules"} inference rules
          %p Formation rules for the type of all propositions:
