              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
          %h2#propositional_impredicativity Propositional impredicativity
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Any universe of propositions satisfying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible type
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Given a universe of propositions
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              itself. Then
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
              says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              has an element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega':\Omega
              such that its type reflection is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              itself. This implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              itself a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
              by definition of universe of proposiions, which implies that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is a contractible type by the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega':\Omega
              and the fact that for all other elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\Omega
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo =
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P = \Omega'
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Any universe of propositions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              closed under the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/empty+type"} empty type
              does not satisfy
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
          %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              Suppose that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is closed under the empty type
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset
              represented in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              by the element
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊥
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot:\Omega
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊥
                    %mo =
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot = \Omega'
              since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mere+proposition"} mere proposition
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ∅
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \emptyset \simeq \Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
              is contractible by propositional impredicativity, the empty type is also contractible, which is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/false"} false
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universe+of+all+propositions"} universe of all propositions
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Prop
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Prop}
              does not satisfy
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
          %h2#directed_univalence Directed univalence
          %p
            Suppose that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            has
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-types"} hom-types
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{hom}_A(a, b)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+univalence"} directed univalence
            for a type of propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ,
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Omega, \mathrm{El})
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo :
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\Omega \vdash \mathrm{El}(P)
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+type+family"} covariant type family
            states that for all propositions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} hom
                    %mi Ω
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{hom}_\Omega(P, Q)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}(P) \to \mathrm{El}(Q)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+extensionality"} propositional extensionality
          %h2#categorical_semantics Categorical semantics
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            of the type of all propositions is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
          %h2#other_types_of_propositions Other types of propositions
          %p There are other types which can also be considered “types of propositions”, that only contain some propositions instead of all propositions. These include
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+booleans"} type of booleans
                = succeed "." do
                  %em decidable propositions
            %li
              %p
                any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dominance"} dominance
                = succeed "," do
                  %em open propositions
                = succeed "." do
                  %em semi-decidable propositions
            %li
              %p
                For a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Russell+universe"} Russell universe
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %mi U
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{A:U} \mathrm{isProp}(A)
                is the type of
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                    \-small propositions
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tarski+universe"} Tarski universe
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (U, T)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mo :
                          %mi U
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isProp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{A:U} \mathrm{isProp}(T(A))
                is the type of
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  \-small propositions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sProp"}> sProp
                , which is the
                %em type of strict propositions
            %li
              %p
                any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+type"} contractible type
                %em type of pointed propositions
                or the
                = succeed "." do
                  %em type of contractible types
          %p
            In general, these types of propositions can also be distinguished between their Russell and Tarski variants, where elements of the type of propositions are actual types, or indices for the type family
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}
          %p
            Most generally, a
            %strong type of propositions
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type"} type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+family"} type family
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            such that
          %ul
            %li
              for every elements
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\Omega
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(P)
              is an
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo :
                          %mi Ω
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo :
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi b
                          %mo :
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi a
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{P:\Omega} \prod_{a:T(P)} \prod_{b:T(P)} a =_{T(P)} b
            %li
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
              function
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} trans
                        %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi P
                      %msub
                        %mo =
                        %mi Ω
                      %mi Q
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{trans}^T(P, Q):P =_\Omega Q \to (T(P) \simeq T(Q))
              %p
                is an equivalence of types for all elements
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P:\Omega
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Q
                      %mo :
                      %mi Ω
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q:\Omega
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo :
                          %mi Ω
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi Q
                          %mo :
                          %mi Ω
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} isEquiv
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} trans
                        %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{P:\Omega} \prod_{Q:\Omega} \mathrm{isEquiv}(\mathrm{trans}^T(P, Q))
          %p
            These axioms imply that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ,
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Omega, T)
            satisfy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+extensionality"} propositional extensionality
            and thus that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+booleans"} type of booleans
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subtype"}> subtype
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject"} subobject
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subobject+classifier"} subobject classifier
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dominance"} dominance
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+extensionality"} propositional extensionality
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+universe"} type universe
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+classes"} type of classes
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+strict+propositions"} type of strict propositions
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+logic+as+a+dependent+type+theory"} propositional logic as a dependent type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+of+entire+relations"} type of entire relations
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+polymorphism"} impredicative polymorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/propositional+impredicativity"} propositional impredicativity
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/impredicative+dependent+type+theory"} impredicative dependent type theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-frame+of+propositions"} sigma-frame of propositions
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#UFP13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Univalent+Foundations+Project"}> Univalent Foundations Project
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopy+Type+Theory+--+Univalent+Foundations+of+Mathematics"} Homotopy Type Theory – Univalent Foundations of Mathematics
              (2013) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://homotopytypetheory.org/book/"}> web
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://hottheory.files.wordpress.com/2013/03/hott-online-323-g28e4374.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            These are called
            %em universe of propositions
            in section 6 of:
          %ul
            %li#AKX25
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thorsten+Altenkirch"}> Thorsten Altenkirch
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ambrus+Kaposi"} Ambrus Kaposi
              = succeed "," do
                %span.newWikiWord
                  Szumi Xie
                  %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Szumi+Xie"} ?
              %em The Groupoid-syntax of Type Theory is a Set
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.14988"}> arXiv:2509.14988
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p The impredicative universe of all propositions and its inference rules are defined in sections 2.8.4 and 5.1.1 of the following draft reference, and the predicate logic of the type theory is defined in section 2.8.5 of:
          %ul
            %li#AngiuliGratzer
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlo+Angiuli"}> Carlo Angiuli
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Gratzer"} Daniel Gratzer
              %em Principles of Dependent Type Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://www.danielgratzer.com/papers/type-theory-book.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Detailed discussion of the type of propositions in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adam+Chlipala"}> Adam Chlipala
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://adam.chlipala.net/cpdt/"} Certified programming with dependent types
              –
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://adam.chlipala.net/cpdt/html/Universes.html"} Library Universes
        .revisedby
